# conf/fleet-env-internal.list — FLEET_* names the scripts read that are NOT
# settings (issue #1101). bin/conf-surface-selftest.sh holds bin/ to: every
# ${FLEET_X:-…} a script reads is either a key in conf/fleet.conf.reference (any @tier,
# including internal) or listed here — so an undocumented knob cannot quietly
# join the config surface again. One name per line, then its kind and a reason:
#   handoff  env one fleet process sets for another (never in a conf)
#   seam     a test-injection point (fake command, fixed clock, sandbox path)
#   path     a state/log/cache location override
#   knob     a hand-override tuning value with a safe in-code default
#   alias    a retired twin of a documented key, still read for old confs
#   legacy / doc  see the reason
# Adding a line here is a decision: a knob an operator would plausibly change
# belongs in conf/fleet.conf.reference (with a tag line) instead.

FLEET_ACCOUNT_ADD_CLAUDE_BIN       seam: the claude binary `fleet account add` runs for `setup-token` (#2084)
FLEET_ACCOUNT_ADD_CODEX_BIN        seam: the codex binary `fleet account add` runs for `login` (#2084)
FLEET_ACCOUNT_LABEL                handoff: the Claude account label a launch was assigned
FLEET_ACCOUNT_PAUSED_CMD           seam: prints the hub client-settings JSON instead of curl (fleet-account.sh quota_paused_fetch, #2083)
FLEET_ACCOUNT_PHASE_WINDOW         knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-account.sh)
FLEET_ACCOUNT_SELECTED             handoff: the account pick already ran for this launch
FLEET_ACCOUNT_TARGET               handoff: the account a migrate/move relaunches on
FLEET_ADMIN_KEY_REPIN              switch: 1 on `fleet node install` re-pins the hub's account-op key in <state>/admin/account.pub (fleet_admin_seat.py ensure, #3696)
FLEET_ADMIN_ROLE                   seam: an existing user standing in for _fleetadmin / fleetadmin (fleet_admin_seat.py, #3696)
FLEET_ADMIN_ROLE_CMD               seam: run in place of each account-making command (fleet_admin_seat.py, #3696)
FLEET_ADMIN_SEAT                   switch: 1 on `fleet node install` sets up the admin role account, its two sudo-able gate copies and sudoers (#3696); 0 takes them away
FLEET_ADMIN_SUDOERS                seam: the sudoers file fleet_admin_seat.py writes (/etc/sudoers.d/fleet-admin, #3696)
FLEET_ADMIN_SVC_CMD                seam: run in place of each launchctl / systemctl for the seat's agent unit (fleet_admin_seat.py agent, #3724)
FLEET_ADMIN_UNIT_DIR               seam: where fleet_admin_seat.py writes the seat's agent unit (/Library/LaunchDaemons | /etc/systemd/system, #3724)
FLEET_ADMIN_VISUDO                 seam: the visudo the new sudoers text is checked with; '' = none (#3696)
FLEET_ADMIT_FORCE_FULL             seam: the drill switch — fleet_machine_admit reads «full» for the one spawn that sets it, so the hub hands it on (T672)
FLEET_ADMIT_GUIDE                  handoff: dash-raw-session tells its own admission this is the pinned /fleet-onboard guide (#3472)
FLEET_ADMIT_OWNER                  handoff: whose admission reservation this process holds (default $$; fleet_admit_*, #2502)
FLEET_AGENTS_BLOCKED               seam: a comma list of agents to treat as blocked by the allowlists, in place of asking the hub (fleet_agent_allow.py, #3826)
FLEET_AGENT_ALLOW_SECS             knob: how long the hub's agent verdict is kept (fleet_agent_allow.py, 60 s, #3826)
FLEET_AGENT_ALLOW_TIMEOUT          knob: how long the agent verdict waits for the hub (fleet_agent_allow.py, 3 s, #3826)
FLEET_ALERTS_ALLCAPPED_SECS        knob: how long an `accounts · all capped` stamp stays an alert (fleet-alerts.sh, 900)
FLEET_ALERTS_EVENT_DEDUP           knob: same kind + text within this many seconds is one alerts event (fleet-alerts.sh event, 60)
FLEET_ALERTS_EVENT_KEEP            knob: how long alerts.events keeps a background event (fleet-alerts.sh, 2592000 = 30 days)
FLEET_ALERTS_EVENT_LIVE            knob: how long a background event counts as a ▲ row before it is popup history (fleet-alerts.sh, 3600)
FLEET_ALERTS_HISTORY_ROWS          knob: how many past events the alerts popup lists (fleet-alerts.sh, 100)
FLEET_ALERTS_HUB_FLASH_SECS        knob: hub unreachable this long before the one hub-lost flash (fleet-alerts.sh, 300)
FLEET_ALERTS_DISK                  seam: 0 skips the alerts producer's own df (a selftest that counts df calls)
FLEET_ALERTS_LOAD_PCT              knob: load per core ×100 that, held FLEET_ALERTS_HOLD_SECS, raises `machine · load high` (fleet-alerts.sh, 90, #1616, T899)
FLEET_ALERTS_LOAD_LO_PCT           knob: load per core ×100 under which, for FLEET_ALERTS_CALM_SECS, `machine · load high` greys (fleet-alerts.sh, 60, T899)
FLEET_ALERTS_MACHINE               knob: 0 turns off the machine load / memory alerts (fleet-alerts.sh, #1616; selftests set it)
FLEET_ALERTS_SERVICES              knob: 0 turns off the registered-service alerts (fleet-alerts.sh `service · failed`, #2526)
FLEET_ALERTS_MEM_PCT               knob: used-memory % that, held FLEET_ALERTS_HOLD_SECS, raises `machine · memory high` (fleet-alerts.sh, 85, #1616, T899)
FLEET_ALERTS_MEM_LO_PCT            knob: used-memory % under which, for FLEET_ALERTS_CALM_SECS, `machine · memory high` greys (fleet-alerts.sh, 80, T899)
FLEET_ALERTS_HOLD_SECS             knob: how long a machine reading must stay over its line before the one warning stands (fleet-alerts.sh, 300, T899)
FLEET_ALERTS_CALM_SECS             knob: how long a machine reading must stay under its low line before the warning greys in place (fleet-alerts.sh, 600, T899)
FLEET_ALERTS_NOW                   seam: the alerts producer's clock (fleet-alerts-selftest.sh drives the machine hold with it)
FLEET_ALERTS_MUTE_SECS             knob: how long `m` in the alerts popup mutes a row (fleet-alerts.sh, 3600)
FLEET_ALERTS_REAUTH_SECS           knob: how old the account.reauth stamp may be before the bar refreshes it through `.fleet-account.py logins` (fleet-alerts.sh, 60)
FLEET_ALERTS_STALL_TTL             knob: how long a forgotten `stalled` alert outlives its killed waiter (fleet-alerts.sh, 21600)
FLEET_ALERTS_TRACE                 knob: how long a cleared alert keeps its ↻ row (fleet-alerts.sh, 1800)
FLEET_ALERTS_TTL                   knob: status-bar refresh interval of alerts.ndjson (fleet-alerts.sh, 5; 0 = every render)
FLEET_ALLOW_CLIENT_TASKS           switch: 1 lets a node the hub typed client still add a repo / turn 承载 on / open a session here (fleet_client_refuse, #4886)
FLEET_ANSWER_POLL                  knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-answer.sh)
FLEET_ANSWER_TIMEOUT               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-answer.sh)
FLEET_ANSWER_HUB_WAIT              knob: seconds fleet-answer.sh waits for a worker_answer on another machine to settle (fleet-answer.sh, 90, #2729)
FLEET_AUTO_RESTORE                 knob: 0 turns off the diskguard tick's fleet-restore.sh --auto pull-up (issue #1784, default on)
FLEET_AUTO_RESTORE_MAX_AGE         knob: --auto skips a fleet whose restore map is older than this many seconds (fleet-restore.sh, 86400)
FLEET_AWAIT_ARMED                  handoff: fleet-await re-exec guard (alarm armed once)
FLEET_AWAIT_CPU_PCT                knob: % of a core above which a `working` child counts as busy, not stalled (fleet-await.sh, 10)
FLEET_AWAIT_TICK                   knob: seconds between ledger-file checks while waiting; a change reads at once (fleet-await.sh, 1, #1272)
FLEET_BASE_DEPS_LOG                path: state/log location override (fleet-deps-link.sh)
FLEET_BASE_DEPS_RETRY_BASE         knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-deps-link.sh)
FLEET_BASE_DEPS_RETRY_CAP          knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-deps-link.sh)
FLEET_BASE_SYNC                    knob: per-repo 0 opts a repo out of base-branch sync
FLEET_BASE_SYNC_LEASE_TTL          knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-base-sync.sh)
FLEET_BG_SOCK                      handoff: the background peer socket a message is sent over
FLEET_BOOTSTRAP_GIT_BASE           seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-login-bootstrap.sh)
FLEET_BOOTSTRAP_DOCTOR             knob: 0 = skip the closing doctor report (fleet-login-new.sh --recycle passes it: 29 s nobody reads, #4044)
FLEET_BOOTSTRAP_FLEET              env handoff: 0 = check the starter out but start no fleet and mark nothing bootstrapped (fleet-home-template.py build, #4194)
FLEET_BOOTSTRAP_CACHE              path: the machine cache a new login installs from; `off` = none (fleet-bootstrap-cache.sh, issue #2297)
FLEET_BREW_LOG                     path: the brew-perms repair log (fleet-brew-perms.sh, #2283)
FLEET_BREW_LOGINS                  seam: how many logins the machine has (fleet-brew-perms.sh, #2283)
FLEET_BREW_ME                      seam: who this login is for the prefix-owner check (fleet-brew-perms.sh, #2283)
FLEET_BREW_PREFIX                  seam: the Homebrew prefix, a sandbox in the drill (fleet-brew-perms.sh, #2283)
FLEET_C                            path: the dash cache root ($TMPDIR/.claude-dash) — tests point it at a sandbox
FLEET_CC_PROJECTS_DIR              path: state/log location override (fleet-migrate.sh)
FLEET_CC_SESSIONS_DIR              path: state/log location override (fleet-lib.sh)
FLEET_CLAUDE_BIN                   path: the claude binary fleet_find_tool tries first (issue #1774)
FLEET_CODEX_BIN                    path: the codex binary bin/fleet-webchat.sh hands the web chat's Codex side first (task R9A2)
FLEET_CLAUDE_COMM                  seam: the process name pane scans treat as Claude
FLEET_CLAUDE_INSTALL_CMD           seam: the Claude Code installer command (fleet-login-bootstrap.sh) — tests swap in a stub
FLEET_CLAUDE_TMP_ROOT              seam: the Claude scratchpad root the listener sweep anchors on (selftest sandbox)
FLEET_CLEAR_CODEX_GAP              knob: seconds fleet-clear-send.sh waits between /clear and Enter in a Codex pane (1, T592)
FLEET_CLEAR_VERIFY_SECS            knob: how long fleet-clear-send.sh waits for the new ledger segment before rc 4 (30, T592)
FLEET_CLIENT                       knob: thin = a bare `fleet` opens the thin client (bin/fleet → fleet-thin.py, #3003) — the person's opt-in until EPIC #2999 C10 makes it the default
FLEET_CLIENT_BEHIND_SECS           knob: how long the hub's /version is kept for the 请更新客户端 check (fleet-client-behind.py, 600 s, #3826)
FLEET_CLIENT_DIR                   path: the shell's state dir the action loop reads (lease, key, where; fleet-thin.py sets it, #1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_KEY_FILE              path: the lease's action key, 0600 (fleet-thin.py sets it; fleet-client-lease.py writes, fleet-client-actions.py reads, #1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_LEASE_CMD             seam: the client-lease command fleet-thin.py / fleet-client-place.sh ask (default python3 fleet-client-lease.py; fleet-thin-selftest.sh swaps in a fake hub, #1715)
FLEET_CLIENT_VER                   handoff: the thin client's .client-version version=, set on the attach command for the home (fleet-thin.py → fleet-remote-view.sh, #3826)
FLEET_CONTROL_AS                   handoff: the agent file a hub-placed start opens as, fleet_control.py → fleet-control-read.sh --as (T672)
FLEET_CLIENT_REHOMED               handoff: the home the thin loop gave up on (换家), set on the attach command for the new home, whose top line says so (fleet-thin.py → fleet-remote-view.sh, T690)
FLEET_DELIVER_HELD                 handoff: the one held delivery code, from the generated agent adapter table (bin/fleet-agent-adapter.sh, T626)
FLEET_DRILL                        handoff: this process is a drill against the live install — fleet_notice.py writes nothing to the person's record (T741)
FLEET_HUB_CLIENT_VERSION           seam: the hub's client_version in place of asking /version (fleet-client-behind.py, #3826)
FLEET_HUB_PAUSE_RETRY_SECS         test seam: pause between the three label reads of fleet-hub-pause.sh (3 s; the drill sets 0, #4621)
FLEET_ID_HUB_POST                  seam: the hub transport `fleet-id.sh push` calls (METHOD PATH, body on stdin → code + body; the selftest's stand-in hub; EPIC T497 C2)
FLEET_ID_LIVE_CMD                  seam: a command printing the live window IDs in place of fleet-id.sh's tmux scan (status / route; EPIC T497 C4)
FLEET_ID_SPAWN                     seam: the spawner `fleet-id.sh continue|reopen --exec` runs in place of dash-raw-session.sh (fleet-id-results-selftest.sh; EPIC T497 C4)
FLEET_ID_PUSH                      knob: 0 = the spawn, the SessionStart hook and result/close do not push the ID ledger to the hub (an explicit push still does; EPIC T497 C2)
FLEET_ID_SWITCH                    seam: on|off in place of the hub's word in ids/.switch (fleet_id.switch_on; fleet-id-migrate-selftest.sh; EPIC T497 C6)
FLEET_KEEP_DEVICE_SECS             knob: fleet-login.py keep — a managed login renews at least this often (default 172800, #4594)
FLEET_KEEP_WALLPAPER               knob: 1 = fleet-wallpaper.sh leaves a headless managed Mac's dynamic desktop as it is (the environment or <state>/machine.env, #4362)
FLEET_MANAGED_CERT_ALERT_CMD       seam: fleet-diskguard.sh managed_cert_watch — the alert it raises (#4594)
FLEET_MANAGED_CERT_EVERY           knob: fleet-diskguard.sh — seconds between a managed login's certificate keep-alive passes (default 900, #4594)
FLEET_MANAGED_CERT_KEEP            knob: 0 turns off a managed login's certificate keep-alive on the diskguard tick (fleet-login.py keep, #4594)
FLEET_DD_FILER                     seam: the filer fleet-durations-drift.sh runs for a drifted durations table (default bin/fleet-ci-say.sh; #4819, #4898)
FLEET_DD_PCT                       CI knob: the per-shard drift (%) past which the nightly files a durations-table refresh (default 20; #4819)
FLEET_MODELCAP_PROBE_BUDGET        knob: seconds one fleet's model-cap probe may take on the reconcile tick (fleet-reconcile-tick.sh, 20)
FLEET_MODELCAP_STREAK              knob: consecutive probe timeouts before fleet-doctor's modelcap row FAILs (fleet-doctor.sh, 3)
FLEET_NODE_ROLE                    seam: managed|client|unknown answers fleet_node_role without asking the hub (#4886)
FLEET_NODE_ROLE_TICK               knob: 0 stops the diskguard tick refreshing the hub's client/managed word (default 1, #4886)
FLEET_NODE_ROLE_TIMEOUT            knob: seconds fleet_node_role waits on GET /v1/node/self (default 4, #4886)
FLEET_NODE_ROLE_TTL                knob: seconds the hub's client/managed word is kept in $FLEET_CONF_DIR/node-role (default 3600, #4886)
FLEET_NOTICE_FORBID                handoff: run-selftests.sh → fleet_notice.py, the message records a test may not write (T741)
FLEET_NOTICE_FORBID_HIT            handoff: run-selftests.sh's per-test marker a refused record write touches (T741)
FLEET_NOTICE_OWN_BOOK              seam: a drill's stand-in for the login's own message record (fleet_notice.py own_book, T741)
FLEET_POPUP_FOLLOW_SECS            knob: how often a frozen popup re-reads its client's window (fleet-popup-lib.sh, T741)
FLEET_POPUP_HOLD_SECS              knob: how often dash-popup.sh --hold checks the panel it holds the popup book for (T890)
FLEET_REAP_NOW_EVERY               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-cleanup-idle.sh --now, T680)
FLEET_REAP_NOW_MAX                 knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-cleanup-idle.sh --now, T680)
FLEET_PLACED                       handoff: @placed (hub | fallback-local) carried to dash-issue-session.sh's --async tail (T672)
FLEET_PLACE_AS                     handoff: a shipped agent file fleet_hub_place sends as `--as` (T672)
FLEET_PLACE_BODY_FILE              handoff: a seeded scratch's words fleet_hub_place sends as `--body-file` (T672)
FLEET_PLACE_NOT_HERE               handoff: this machine's own admission refusal fleet_hub_place sends as `--not-here` (T672)
FLEET_RENEW_BELOW_SECS             knob: a USE renews the connection certificate when less than this many seconds are left — `fleet` before it connects, ssh to a fleet machine, the client keeper before its hub read (fleet-login.py renew --on-use, fleet-connect.py, the thin client; 8640 = 20% of 12h, #3701)
FLEET_CLIENT_LIST_FILE             path: the person's clients as the hub last said (fleet-client-lease.py writes, the top line reads, #1932)
FLEET_DEPS_SHARE_CLONE             seam: off = this filesystem cannot clone, copy = plain cp -R (fleet-deps-share.sh, #3403)
FLEET_DEPS_SHARE_LOG               path: state/log location override (fleet-deps-share.sh)
FLEET_DEPS_SHARE_TIMEOUT           knob: wall-clock budget for one worktree's share pass (fleet-lib.sh fleet_worktree_deps_share, 60)
FLEET_DISPATCH_AGENTS_HERE         seam: the agents installed here, comma-separated, for ⌘T's agent step (fleet-quick-dispatch.py, #3004)
FLEET_DISPATCH                     handoff: resolved coding provider and accepted request/task identity across spawn adapters (#4392)
FLEET_DISPATCH_RESULT              handoff: ccquota place writes the hub's accepted dispatch to this caller-owned temporary file (#4392)
FLEET_LAUNCH                       legacy: retired with the launch proof / start reservation (EPIC T497 C8) — a session started before it still carries it; fleet_repo_authority.py strips it at a start
FLEET_LAUNCH_CONTEXT               legacy: retired with the launch proof / start reservation (EPIC T497 C8) — a session started before it still carries it; fleet_repo_authority.py strips it at a start
FLEET_LAUNCH_CREATE                legacy: retired with the launch proof / start reservation (EPIC T497 C8) — a session started before it still carries it; fleet_repo_authority.py strips it at a start
FLEET_ROLLBACK_GH                  seam: the gh command bin/fleet-release-rollback.sh runs (#4663)
FLEET_ID_DIR                       path: the ID ledgers dir ($FLEET_CONF_DIR/ids — fleet_id.py ledger_dir; fleet_cfg_work_over, T569)
FLEET_TASK_CLOSED_CMD              seam: answers `<T<n>>` instead of fleet_task_control.py closed — 0 closed · 1 open · 3 unknown (fleet_task_closed, fleet-cleanup-idle.py, #4897)
FLEET_TASK_PARK_CMD                seam: run as `<T<n>>` instead of fleet-task-record.sh set --parked when the idle reaper parks a session waiting on its person (fleet-cleanup-idle.py, E101)
FLEET_TASK_DUP_OK                  knob: 1 = dash-raw-session.sh opens a window for a record a window here already runs (T847 refuses by default)
FLEET_TASK_RECORD                  seam: the task-record script fleet-brief.sh asks `get T<n>` of (#4897, #4898)
FLEET_TASK_FID                     handoff: `T<n>=<ID>` — the task's own ID fleet-task-record.sh dispatch hands its spawner, read only for that record (fleet_task_fid; EPIC T644 C2)
FLEET_TASK_FID_TIMEOUT             knob: seconds the spawner waits on the hub for a task's ID (fleet_task_fid / fleet_task_take; default 5; EPIC T644 C2)
FLEET_LAUNCH_SUPERVISOR            legacy: retired with the launch proof / start reservation (EPIC T497 C8) — a session started before it still carries it; fleet_repo_authority.py strips it at a start
FLEET_LAUNCH_NATIVE                legacy: retired with the launch proof / start reservation (EPIC T497 C8) — a session started before it still carries it; fleet_repo_authority.py strips it at a start
FLEET_LAUNCH_DELIVERY              legacy: retired with the launch proof / start reservation (EPIC T497 C8) — a session started before it still carries it; fleet_repo_authority.py strips it at a start
FLEET_PLACE_REQUEST_ID             handoff: stable client placement key across lease reacquisition (#4392)
FLEET_DISPATCH_GO_CMD              seam: replaces fleet-view-go.sh when a 看台's ⌘T goes to the window it opened (fleet-quick-dispatch.py, #3097)
FLEET_ENTRY                        knob: a managed machine's entry port on/off — machine.env (root 0600), written by `fleet node install`, not a fleet.conf key (#3070)
FLEET_ENTRY_PORT                   knob: the entry port's port (22022) — machine.env beside FLEET_ENTRY (#3070)
FLEET_ENTRY_MACHINE_PORT           knob: a second port the entry sshd also listens on — the machine's own, for the router's per-machine forward; machine.env beside FLEET_ENTRY, written by `fleet node install` (T743)
FLEET_ENTRY_BOOK                   handoff: the entry sshd's SetEnv to fleet-entry.sh — the entry book (root 0644) that names each key (#3071)
FLEET_ENTRY_VIEW                   seam: the drill's 看台 stand-in for fleet-entry.sh, set only through FLEET_ENTRY_TEST_SETENV under FLEET_NODE_TEST (#3071)
FLEET_POOL_SESSION_CRED            seam: the stand-in fleet-session-cred.sh for fleet-pool-run.sh (task KEA0)
FLEET_SHELL_POOL                   knob: 0 = claude / codex typed at a managed login's shell run plain, this shell only (fleet-pool-run.sh, task KEA0)
FLEET_ENTRY_PORTMAP                knob: auto (NAT-PMP, then UPnP) | off — whether `entry reach` asks the home's router to forward the entry port; machine.env beside FLEET_ENTRY (#3072)
FLEET_ENTRY_REACH_SECS             knob: how long `entry reach` waits for the hub's dials (30 s) (#3072)
FLEET_ENTRY_REACH_EVERY            knob: how often the cluster door's resident loop runs `entry reach` (300 s; 0 = off) — a door has no node program to (#4112)
