FLEET_TRANSFER_BOOT_WAIT           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-transfer.sh)
FLEET_TRANSFER_EXIT_WAIT           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-transfer.sh)
FLEET_TRANSFER_IDLE_WAIT           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-transfer.sh)
FLEET_TRANSFER_ROLLBACK_HOLD       knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-transfer.sh)
FLEET_TRANSFER_RETRYING            handoff: fleet-transfer.sh --retry tells its child run not to record a retry of its own (#1669)
FLEET_TRASH_PURGE_URGENT           handoff: the cleanup daemon marks an urgent trash purge (skips the load cap)
FLEET_TRASH_SWEEP_BUDGET           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-cleanup-daemon.sh)
FLEET_UI_QUIET                     handoff: 1 = fleet_ui_fail draws nothing — the caller re-says the failure in its own one line (issue #1618)
FLEET_UPDATE_ROOT                  path: the install fleet-update.sh reports on (default its own ../, #1805)
FLEET_WINDOW_REAP                  knob: 0 turns the close-time orphan-tree sweep off (fleet-window-reap.sh; read from the tmux server env, not a conf)
FLEET_WINDOW_REAP_EXEMPT_RE        knob: extra argv ERE the close-time sweep never reaps (fleet_orphan_trees)
FLEET_WINDOW_REAP_FG               handoff: fleet-window-reap.sh --hook re-execs itself detached with this set
FLEET_WINDOW_REAP_PASSES           knob: seconds after a close to sweep at (fleet-window-reap.sh, "2 6 20")
FLEET_WINDOW_REAP_ROOT             seam: narrow the close-time sweep to tops whose cwd is under this dir (selftests)
FLEET_WORKER_PROMPT_FILE           alias: retired twin of FLEET_WORKER_PROMPT="@<path>" (#1101) — still read, wins when set
FLEET_WORKTREE_SETUP_LOG           path: state/log location override (fleet-lib.sh)
FLEET_WRAP_FAST_FAIL               knob: an agent ending within this many seconds is a launch failure the wrapper passes through (fleet-session-wrap.sh, 5)
FLEET_WRAP_LAUNCH                  seam: the launcher fleet-session-wrap.sh runs (default bin/fleet-claude.sh)
FLEET_WT_PENDING                   handoff: the cold start's checkout marker (the filler's pid) a new window's agent carries; set-claude-state.sh waits on it (#2237)
FLEET_X                            doc: the placeholder name in a comment, not a key
FLEET_SHOW_OUT                     test seam: where fleet-show-send.py writes instead of /dev/tty (fleet-show-selftest.sh, #1367)
FLEET_OPEN_ACTIONS_BIN             seam: the client-action sender fleet-open.sh runs (default fleet-client-actions.py, #1717)
FLEET_OPEN_CLIENT                  knob: 0 = fleet-open.sh skips the person's client (hub / this screen) and goes the terminal road (1, #1717)
FLEET_OPEN_CLIENT_WAIT             knob: seconds fleet-open.sh waits for the client's answer before saying queued (5, #1717)
FLEET_OPEN_LOCAL_CMD               seam: the local opener fleet-open.sh runs when the client is on this screen (default open / xdg-open, #1717)
FLEET_OPEN_WHERE_CMD               seam: the where read fleet-open.sh / fleet-show.sh run (default fleet-client-where.sh, #1717)
FLEET_OPEN_ACK_WAIT                knob: seconds fleet-open.sh waits for the far side's receipt before saying unconfirmed (12, #3538)
FLEET_OPEN_RELAY_CMD               seam: the peer runner fleet-open.sh hands a home's open to (default fleet-peerlink.py exec, #3538)
FLEET_OPEN_FWD_CMD                 seam: the forwarder a home's fleet-open.sh --from-peer runs (default fleet-peerlink.py fwd, #3538)
FLEET_OPEN_PROBE_LOOPBACK          knob: 0 = fleet-open-addr.py never maps this machine's tailnet URL to a port found listening on 127.0.0.1 (1, #3538)
FLEET_OPEN_PAGE_SECS               knob: seconds a forwarded page stays forwarded — the thin loop's and the home's peer forward (1800, #3236/#3538)
FLEET_SHOW_ACTIONS_BIN             seam: the client-action sender fleet-show.sh runs (default fleet-client-actions.py, #1717)
FLEET_SHOW_CLIENT                  knob: 0 = fleet-show.sh skips the person's client and goes the terminal road (1, #1717)
FLEET_SHOW_CLIENT_WAIT             knob: seconds fleet-show.sh waits for the client's answer per file (10, #1717)
FLEET_SHOW_LOCAL_CMD               seam: the local opener fleet-show.sh runs when the client is on this screen (default open / xdg-open, #1717)
FLEET_OPEN_SECRET_FILE             seam: the shared secret's path (fleet-open-selftest.sh, #1379)
FLEET_OPEN_URL_BIN                 seam: the fallback opener instead of bin/open-url.sh (fleet-open-selftest.sh, #1379)
FLEET_LOOP_BACKFILL_BYTES          knob: internal budget, transcript tail bytes the Stop hook replays to backfill a pre-hook @loop (fleet_stop_wait, 262144, #1370)
FLEET_WAIT_REEVAL                  knob: 0 turns off the idle-window re-ask of done ↔ looping + @claude_wait (fleet-wait-reeval.sh, on, #1376)
FLEET_TOOL_WAIT                    knob: 0 turns off the `tool` wait reason — a fleet tool call in flight no longer holds a window busy (fleet_window_tool_busy, on, #1880)
FLEET_HUMAN_WAIT                   knob: 0 turns off the `human` wait reason — a person mid-scan no longer holds reopen / handoff (fleet_window_human, on, #2869)
FLEET_HUB_CACHE_SECS               knob: internal budget, seconds the hub worker cache (control/hub-workers.tsv) stays fresh for fleet_worker_locate (30, #1420)
FLEET_HUB_STATUS_CMD               seam: command printing `<worker_id>\t<node>` that refreshes the hub worker cache; the ccquota agent now writes the cache itself (#1421); kept for a hub reached some other way (fleet_worker_locate, #1420)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_CMD             seam: command printing the hub's fleet_sessions JSON instead of GET $CCQUOTA_HUB_URL/v1/fleet/fleet_sessions (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, #1423)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_EVERY           knob: internal pacing, seconds between the remote-sessions refreshes (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 10, #1423)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_IDLE_EVERY      knob: internal pacing, seconds between a NODE loop's refreshes while no client is attached anywhere — napped 2 s at a time, ended by a client attaching (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 30; an explicit FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_EVERY is used instead, #4261)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_WATCHED_EVERY   knob: internal pacing, seconds between the refreshes while a client is attached to any session of this fleet — the loop sends If-None-Match so an unchanged hub answers 304 (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 2, #1481)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_WAIT            knob: internal pacing, seconds the hub may hold a watched fleet_sessions ask (long poll) until a heartbeat moves its ETag — capped at 25, under an ingress's 60 s idle timeout (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 25, #1526)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_LONGPOLL        knob: 0 = the watched loop never sends `wait` and keeps its fixed 2 s cadence (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 1, #1526)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_STATUS_STALE    knob: seconds of hub_ok age past which `fleet-hub-sessions.sh --status` (fleet-doctor's hub-sessions row) reports the refresh stalled (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 60, #1596)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_LOOP_SECS       knob: internal budget, how long one detached refresh loop lives before the next collector tick restarts it (70, #1423)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_STALE           knob: internal budget, seconds of hub silence (global/hub_ok, else the cache's #ts) after which the dash reads every remote row as 失联, the bar `入口 ○`, and a remote-row action refuses — fleet_status_hub_lost in fleet-status-lib.sh (60, #1423 #1483)
FLEET_REMOTE_BIN                   knob: the fleet's bin/ on the other machine, default .claude/fleet/bin (fleet-peerlink.py, fleet-open.sh, fleet-session-cli.py, #1424)
FLEET_REMOTE_SSH_CMD               seam: the ssh program another machine is reached with (fleet-peerlink.py, fleet-client-upload.py)
FLEET_HUB_URL                      handoff: the hub URL `fleet connect` (fleet-connect.py) reads (#1424)
FLEET_SHELL                        handoff: 1 = a reader sourcing fleet.conf takes its [client] section, else [node] (fleet-conf.sh's guards; set for the read by fleet-client-update.sh, fleet-update.sh, fleet-release-lib.sh, fleet_keys.py, #1623)
FLEET_SHELL_SESSION                knob: the shell's tmux session + socket label (fleet-install.sh, default fleet-shell, #1484)
FLEET_SHELL_CACHE                  path: the shell's own cache root — its bin/ mirror, tmux.conf and $TMPDIR (bin/fleet, fleet-client-update.sh, ~/.cache/claude-fleet/shell, #1484)
FLEET_HOME_FIRST_OPENING_MAX       knob: seconds first_session keeps waiting, uncounted, while the hub says the newcomer's login is opening (fleet-thin.py, 2400, #2941)
FLEET_CONNECT_ROUTE_FILE           handoff: its caller → fleet-connect.py, where the chosen route is written for the pane (#1628)
FLEET_CONNECT_LOGIN                handoff: its caller → fleet-connect.py, the login a session's fleet runs under — ssh -l <it> (#2430)
FLEET_CONNECT_RETEST               handoff: its caller → fleet-connect.py, last = the remembered route first on a reconnect (#2886), 1 = re-measure every route (the upgrade, #1628)
FLEET_CONNECT_UPGRADE_SECS         knob: on the hub relay, seconds between direct probes (15, #1628)
FLEET_REMOTE_ORPHAN_SECS           knob: age before a registered attach with no tmux client counts as an orphan (60, #1907)
FLEET_REMOTE_ORPHAN_REAP           knob: 0 = an attach never reaps orphaned attaches; health still counts them (1, #1907)
FLEET_VIEW_LANG                    handoff: the language a 看台's client brought through the door (@view_lang), in the 看台 session's environment for fleet-ui-lang.sh; set (even empty) = it decides after the person's choice (fleet-remote-view.sh, #3329)
FLEET_UI_PERSON_FILE               seam: the person-bundle.json fleet-ui-lang.sh reads the person's ui_lang from (default $FLEET_CONF_DIR/person-bundle.json, #3329)
FLEET_VIEW_FIRST_CMD               seam: replaces `fleet-quickopen.py` when attach --thin lands a 看台 with no orchestrator here on ⌘N's road (`do new`) (fleet-remote-view.sh, #3007)
FLEET_VIEW_KEEP_SECS               knob: seconds a thin client's 看台 (attach --thin) outlives its client for --resume before prune takes it (600, #2763)
FLEET_ID_BACKFILL_CMD              seam: a shell command printing the live windows `fleet-id.sh backfill` reads (socket · @fleet_id · window · @cc_agent · repo · worktree · task · session ids · role, tab-separated) instead of tmux (EPIC T497 C17)
FLEET_VIEW_PR_TIMEOUT              knob: seconds ⌘P's row menu waits on the hub for a task record's PR (fleet_view.py task_pr, #4902)
FLEET_VIEW_ROWS_CMD                seam: a shell command printing the 看台 switcher's rows instead of tmux-dashboard-rows.sh --rows (fleet_view.py, #3000)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_USER            knob: whose sessions on the other machines the dash shows (os_user; default `id -un`, `*` = every login the hub shows; #1423)
FLEET_CERT                         handoff: the connection-certificate key pair a sidebar / `fleet connect` signs with — the key; `<key>-cert.pub` beside it (default ~/.ssh/fleet-cert, what `fleet login` wrote; fleet-hub-sessions.sh, fleet-connect.py, #1475)
FLEET_HUB_LEASE_CMD                seam: the hub issue-lease command (default `ccquota lease`), run as `<cmd> acquire|release [--force] <repo> <issue> <worker_id>` (fleet_hub_lease, #1422)
FLEET_HUB_RETAIN_SECS              knob: internal budget, seconds a hub worker map may age before remote children stop holding their parent (600, #1421)
FLEET_HUB_CURL                     seam: the transport fleet-node-maintenance.sh calls the hub with (default `curl`; the selftest's fake records argv + body; #1427)
FLEET_HUB_TIMEOUT                  knob: seconds fleet-node-maintenance.sh waits on one hub call (curl --max-time), default 15 (#1427)
FLEET_HUB_PLACE_CMD                seam: the hub placement command (default `ccquota place`), run as `<cmd> --node <n> [--origin-wid <w>] [--agent <a>] <repo> <issue> <worker_id>` (fleet_hub_place, #1425)
FLEET_HUB_MOVE_CMD                 seam: the hub session-move command (default `ccquota move`), run as `<cmd> plan|send [<flag>…] <repo> <worker_id>` (fleet_hub_move, #1426)
FLEET_HUB_WRITE_CMD                seam: command run as `<cmd> <tool> <args_json>` in place of the hub write doors (viewer-token POST /v1/fleet/<tool>, device-signed POST /v1/fleet/write) — the sidebar selftest records what the remote-row menu writes (fleet-hub-write.sh, #1487)
FLEET_HUB_NODE_SUDO                seam: the privilege prefix `fleet-hub-node.sh env --write` reads a root-owned agent plist with (default `sudo -n`; empty = none) (#1491)
FLEET_HUB_NODE_DAEMON_DIR          seam: where `fleet-hub-node.sh env --write` looks for the system LaunchDaemon com.ccquota.agent.<login>.plist (default /Library/LaunchDaemons) (#1491)
FLEET_JOIN_SUDO                    seam: the privilege prefix fleet-node-join.sh uses for package installs / system units (default `sudo -n`; empty = none) (#1418)
FLEET_JOIN_OS                      seam: overrides `uname -s` in fleet-node-join.sh (darwin|linux) (#1418)
FLEET_JOIN_ARCH                    seam: overrides `uname -m` in fleet-node-join.sh (#1418)
FLEET_JOIN_POLL                    seam: seconds between fleet-node-join.sh's /v1/node/self polls (default 3) (#1418)
FLEET_JOIN_CREDSEP                 seam: the fleet-credsep.sh fleet-node-join.sh writes a separated login's node.env through (default: beside it, else the install's) (#2316)
FLEET_NODE_STATE                   path: com.claude-fleet.node's state dir (default /var/db/fleet-node) — fleet_node_manages reads its accounts.json (#2332); fleet-login-remove.sh reads logins/<login>/services (#2528)
FLEET_NODE_JOIN_ARGS               seam: extra fleet-node-join.sh options `fleet node join` passes through (fleet-node-selftest: --no-deps --service detached …) (#1627)
FLEET_NODE_ROOT                    path: the managed machine's root runtime dir (default /Library/Application Support/claude-fleet) — fleet-node-install.sh / fleet-node-update.py (#2330, #2334)
FLEET_NODE_CORE                    switch: the root core (#3555) — 1 on `fleet node install` installs com.claude-fleet.node-core, 0 removes it; 0 in the environment = every caller takes the old road (fleet_node_core.available)
FLEET_NODE_TEST                    seam: 1 = the machine daemon's tools run without root in a sandbox (fleet-node-install.sh, fleet-node-supervisor.py, #2330)
FLEET_NODE_LOG                     path: com.claude-fleet.node's log dir (default /var/log/fleet-node) — fleet-service.sh `logs -f` reads logins/<login>/<name>.log under it (#2525)
FLEET_NODE_SUPERVISOR              seam: the supervisor fleet-service.sh hands the register to (default the root runtime's bin/fleet-node-supervisor.py, #2525)
FLEET_SERVICE_LOGIN                seam: the login fleet-service.sh registers for (default `id -un`, #2525)
FLEET_SERVICE_SUDO                 seam: how fleet-service.sh becomes root (default `sudo -n`; empty = run directly, #2525)
FLEET_SERVICE                      handoff: the register entry's name, set by com.claude-fleet.node for a service / task it runs — fleet-task-run.sh names its log lines with it (#2525, #2529)
FLEET_TASK_PROMPT                  handoff: an agent task's prompt ({date} filled), com.claude-fleet.node → fleet-task-run.sh (#2529)
FLEET_TASK_WINDOW                  handoff: the session's window name for this attempt (-<n> on a retry), daemon → fleet-task-run.sh (#2529)
FLEET_TASK_DONE_FILE               handoff: done_when.file, the output a run must leave (empty = opening the session is success), daemon → fleet-task-run.sh (#2529)
FLEET_TASK_TIMEOUT                 handoff: the entry's timeout (s) for a run with a done file, daemon → fleet-task-run.sh (#2529)
FLEET_TASK_IDLE                    handoff: the entry's idle (s): a session not working that long without its done file has failed, daemon → fleet-task-run.sh (#2529)
FLEET_TASK_REAP                    knob: an agent task session's reap policy (default done:15m), spawned --reap-origin probe so a finished turn closes it (fleet-task-run.sh, T862)
FLEET_TASK_FLEET                   handoff: the entry's fleet (empty = the login's only one), daemon → fleet-task-run.sh (#2529)
FLEET_TASK_ATTEMPT                 handoff: the attempt number of this slot, daemon → fleet-task-run.sh (#2529)
FLEET_TASK_SLOT                    handoff: the slot's day (YYYY-MM-DD), daemon → fleet-task-run.sh (#2529)
FLEET_TASK_BARK_CRED               handoff: the credential NAME holding the entry's Bark key (the value is injected under that name), daemon → fleet-task-run.sh --notify (#2529)
FLEET_TASK_SPAWN                   seam: the spawner fleet-task-run.sh opens the session with (default the login's ~/.claude/fleet/bin/dash-raw-session.sh; an entry's --env, #2529)
FLEET_TASK_POLL                    seam: seconds between fleet-task-run.sh's looks at a session waiting for its done file (default 30, #2529)
FLEET_TASK_NOTIFY                  handoff: the Bark message of a failed task, daemon → fleet-task-run.sh --notify (#2529)
FLEET_TASK_BARK_URL                seam: the Bark server fleet-task-run.sh --notify pushes to (default https://api.day.app, #2529)
FLEET_NODE_CLOCK                   seam: a file holding an epoch — the agent tasks' schedule clock in fleet-node-supervisor.py's selftests (FLEET_NODE_TEST=1 only, #2529)
FLEET_NODE_TASK_CATCHUP            pacing: how late (s) com.claude-fleet.node still runs a missed agent-task slot, e.g. after a reboot (default 21600, #2529)
FLEET_NODE_INSTALL_CURL            seam: the curl fleet-node-install.sh talks to the hub with (selftests: a fake hub, #2330)
FLEET_NODE_CLIENT                  hatch: 1 = bin/fleet on a managed machine takes the device client's road (a resident client from before #2702 still there), not the node-hosted one (#2720)
FLEET_NODE_HOSTED                  handoff: 1 = the client runs ON a managed machine for one ssh (bin/fleet → fleet-client-lease.py via node-hosted; #2720)
FLEET_NODE_HOSTED_CACHE            path: the node-hosted client's temp cache (default $TMPDIR/fleet-node-client-<uid>, #2720)
FLEET_NODE_RUNTIME                 path: the managed machine's runtime link (default /Library/Application Support/claude-fleet/current) — the node-hosted client runs from its bin/ (#2720)
FLEET_RETIRE_GRACE                 pacing: seconds fleet-node-shell-retire.sh waits between TERM and KILL for a client process (default 3, #2702)
FLEET_RETIRE_QUIT_WAIT             pacing: seconds fleet-node-shell-retire.sh gives the login's own `fleet quit` (default 20, #2702)
FLEET_RETIRE_OLD                   hatch: 0 = bare `fleet` leaves the deleted two-pane client running instead of retiring it unattended in the background (default 1, #4283)
FLEET_NODE_INSTALL_OS              seam: overrides `uname -s` in fleet-node-install.sh (#2330)
FLEET_NODE_INSTALL_ARCH            seam: overrides `uname -m` in fleet-node-install.sh (#2330)
FLEET_NODE_PYTHON                  seam: the python3 fleet-node-install.sh runs (default /usr/bin/python3, #2330)
FLEET_NODE_SSH_DIR                 seam: where fleet-node-install.sh writes the hub's ssh CA + sshd_config.d drop-in (default /etc/ssh, #2330)
FLEET_NODE_SSHD                    seam: the sshd fleet-node-install.sh checks with (`-t` / `-T`; default /usr/sbin/sshd, '' = no check, #2330)
FLEET_NODE_SEAT                    switch: 1 on `fleet node install` moves the node daemon onto its own account _fleetnode / fleetnode (install --seat, #3668)
FLEET_NODE_SEAT_AGENT              switch: 1 on `fleet node install` runs the node program as the seat too (install --seat --agent, #3669); 0 puts it back on root
FLEET_NODE_SEAT_CMD                seam: a program run in place of each account-making command (seat_make, #3668)
FLEET_NODE_SEAT_NAME               seam: the seat account's name (an existing user; default _fleetnode / fleetnode, #3668)
FLEET_NODE_PASSWD                  test seam: a JSON {login: {uid, gid, home}} read instead of this machine's accounts (fleet-node-supervisor.py seat_ident, fleet-node-install.sh seat_there — #3810)
FLEET_NODE_CORE_WAIT               pacing: seconds `fleet-node-core.py install` waits for the new core's socket to answer before it puts the old unit back (default 15, #3810)
FLEET_NODE_SEATED                  seam: (FLEET_NODE_TEST only) this supervisor is the seated daemon (#3668)
FLEET_NODE_SERVICE                 handoff: installer selects systemd or foreground supervision on Linux (#3022)
FLEET_NODE_ACCOUNT_OPS             knob: 1 = a Linux managed machine's node program opens / closes its own logins for the hub (CapLoginJoin); machine.env, written by fleet node install on Linux (#3210)
FLEET_NODE_UPDATE_OWNER            handoff: image disables runtime self-updates in ACK; Kubernetes owns the pinned image (#3022)
FLEET_NODE_UPDATE_BACKWARD         hatch: =1 lets fleet-node-update.py switch to a target older than the running release (a machine only moves forward otherwise, #4671)
FLEET_NODE_PROFILE                 handoff: render.py sets user-pod / door on a cluster pod; fleet-node-install.sh reads it for a person's pod (#3550, #3757)
FLEET_POD_LOGIN                    handoff: render.py --login — the one login a person's pod is made for; its node runs as it (#3757)
FLEET_POD_UID                      handoff: render.py --uid — that login's number, the fleet container's runAsUser (#3757)
FLEET_HUB_INTERNAL_URL             handoff: render.py --hub-internal on a person's pod / svc run: the hub's in-cluster Service its machine-to-hub calls dial; FLEET_HUB_URL stays the identity (#4175)
FLEET_USER_POD                     handoff: render.py --user-pod sets 1 on a person's pod; install-apply writes FLEET_MACHINE_TASKS=off for its login (#3550, #3734)
FLEET_NODE_RUN_SSHD                handoff: foreground supervisor owns the container SSH daemon (#3022)
FLEET_NODE_SYSTEMCTL               seam: Linux systemd command for supervisor and SSH CA reload (#3022)
FLEET_NODE_DAEMON_DIR              path: the LaunchDaemons dir the supervisor manages (selftests: a temp dir, #2336)
FLEET_NODE_USERS                   path: the home-directory root the supervisor reads LaunchAgents under (selftests: a temp dir, #2336)
FLEET_HUB_NODES_CMD                seam: command printing the hub's /v1/nodes JSON instead of a GET (fleet-hub-sessions.sh refresh_summaries, #1482)
FLEET_HUB_LIMITS_CMD               seam: command printing the hub's /v1/limits?account=all JSON instead of a GET (fleet-hub-sessions.sh refresh_summaries, #1482)
FLEET_HUB_PROGRESS                 knob: 0 turns the hub progress pull off (fleet-hub-node.sh progress exits 3; #1648)
FLEET_STATUS_G                     path: the status bar's cache dir (global/, where hub_nodes / hub_limits / remote_<sess> live) — a selftest sandbox (fleet-status-lib.sh, #1482)
FLEET_HUB_SUMMARY_EVERY            knob: seconds between the status-bar summaries (/v1/nodes + /v1/limits) a refresh round fetches, 0 = every round (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 10, #1482)
FLEET_DOCTOR_AGENT_TARGET          seam: the target the doctor's `agent` line compares against instead of `stable` (fleet-doctor.sh → fleet-node-upgrade.sh --status, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_DAEMON_DIR      seam: where fleet-node-upgrade.sh finds the com.ccquota.agent.<login>.plist LaunchDaemons (default /Library/LaunchDaemons) (#1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_AGENT_DIR       seam: where fleet-node-upgrade.sh finds this login's com.ccquota.agent.plist LaunchAgent (default ~/Library/LaunchAgents) (#1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_PS              seam: command printing `uid pid path` rows instead of ps (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_UIDS            seam: "login=uid …" consulted before `id -u` (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_SUDO            seam: the privilege prefix for install / kickstart (default `sudo -n`; empty = none) (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_LAUNCHCTL       seam: the launchctl binary (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_NODES_CMD       seam: command printing the hub's /v1/nodes JSON instead of a GET (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_HOSTNAME        seam: overrides `hostname -s` — which /v1/nodes rows are this machine's (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_OS              seam: overrides `uname -s` (fleet-node-upgrade.sh is launchd-only, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_POLL            seam: seconds between post-restart hub polls (default 2) (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_PEER_CERT                    escape hatch: 0 = never ask the hub for a machine-to-machine certificate, plain ssh (fleet-peer-cert.sh, #1626)
FLEET_PEER_CERT_SECS               seam: life asked for a peer certificate (default 300; the hub caps it at 300) (fleet-peer-cert.sh, #1626)
FLEET_PEER_CERT_MARGIN             knob: seconds before expiry a cached peer certificate stops being reused (fleet-peer-cert.sh, 30, #1631)
FLEET_PEER_CERT_CONNECT_SECS       seam: connect bound for the peer-cert request — a down hub is refused inside 1 s (default 0.8) (fleet-peer-cert.sh, #1630)
FLEET_PEER_LIST_CONNECT_SECS       seam: connect bound for the /v1/node/peers request (default 2) (fleet-peer-list.sh, #3482)
FLEET_PEER_KEY                     path: the peer key the hub signs (default ~/.ssh/fleet-peer) (fleet-peer-cert.sh, #1626)
FLEET_CLIENT_AUTO_UPDATE           escape hatch: 0 = the installed client never updates itself from the hub; the team's defaults still land (fleet-client-update.sh, #1722)
FLEET_CLIENT_CHECK_SECS            knob: seconds between a client start's checks with the hub (fleet-client-update.sh, 3600, #1722)
FLEET_CLIENT_ROOT                  path: the installed client's home (default the script's ../) (fleet-client-update.sh, #1722)
FLEET_CLIENT_STATE                 path: the client update's stamp / log / bar note dir (default ~/.cache/claude-fleet/client) (fleet-client-update.sh, #1722)
FLEET_CLIENT_TIMEOUT               seam: seconds per hub request on a client start (default 3) (fleet-client-update.sh, #1722)
FLEET_CLIENT_UPDATED               env handoff: bin/fleet re-execs the switched client once with it set, so it never loops (#1722)
FLEET_CLIENT_UPDATE_STATE          path: the client's update.state (default <shell cache>/update.state; the selftests' sandbox, #1781)
FLEET_INSTALL_NODE_UPGRADE         seam: the fleet-node-upgrade.sh an install-sync tick drives (default $ROOT/bin/…) (fleet-install-sync.sh, #1723)
FLEET_INSTALL_NODE_SUDO_CHECK      seam: the command that says sudo -n works, so this login upgrades LaunchDaemon logins (default `sudo -n true`) (fleet-install-sync.sh, #1723)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_DIST_CMD        seam: stands in for the --dist curl — `<cmd> <os-arch> <body> <headers>` prints the HTTP code (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1723)
FLEET_CFG_RESTART_MIGRATE          seam: the fleet-migrate.sh a stale-config reopen hands its window to (fleet-cfg-restart.sh, #1783)
FLEET_WORKER_CRED                  handoff: the session's worker credential, minted per launch by fleet-session-wrap.sh for the fleet tool service — env only, never written down (fleet-mcp.py, #1809)
FLEET_CODEX_LAUNCHER_PID           handoff: the Codex launcher's pid, exported by fleet-codex.sh — marks a Codex pane to its hooks (fleet-codex-session.py, fleet-where-hook.sh #1954)
FLEET_WORKER_ASSERT                handoff: a session's own hub worker assertion (fleet-mcp.py, #1810); fleet-session-cred.sh borrows a hub pass with it (#1972)
FLEET_HUB_POOL_SECS                knob: seconds between a node's asks for the hub's pool settings (fleet-hub-pool.sh, 300, #2029)
FLEET_HUB_POOL_TIMEOUT             knob: curl timeout for that ask (fleet-hub-pool.sh, 5s, #2029)
FLEET_SKIP_HUB_POOL                seam: fleet-lib skips hub-pool.env (fleet-hub-pool.sh status: what this machine sets alone)
FLEET_MACOS_WATCH                  knob: 0 turns off the red-master-macOS alert on the diskguard tick (fleet-macos-watch.sh, fleet-diskguard.sh, #2286, #3120)
FLEET_MACOS_WATCH_SECS             knob: internal pacing, seconds between two reads of master's macOS runs per repo (fleet-macos-watch.sh, default 600, #2286)
FLEET_MACOS_WORKFLOW               knob: the workflow file whose macOS shard jobs the watcher reads (fleet-macos-watch.sh, fleet-diskguard.sh, default selftests-macos.yml since #4663 — mac-follow.yml before, #3869, #2286)
FLEET_MACOS_PUSH_NIGHTS            knob: red nights in a macOS streak before the ONE push to the person over FLEET_NOTIFY_CMD (fleet-macos-watch.sh, default 2, T889)
FLEET_MACOS_NOTIFY_CMD             seam: what the watcher runs instead of FLEET_NOTIFY_CMD for its one push (selftests, T889)
FLEET_MACOS_WATCH_WALK             knob: internal pacing, how many of the newest runs the watcher reads jobs of looking for a macOS verdict (fleet-macos-watch.sh, default 25, #3143)
FLEET_MACOS_BRANCH                 knob: the branch whose macOS runs the watcher reads (fleet-macos-watch.sh, default master, #2286)
